#!/bin/sh
# Fake kubectl for hack/migration-57-foundationdb-version.bats. It serves only
# the calls migration 57 (and lib/cozystack-version.sh) make and appends one
# line per call to $FAKE_CMDLOG.
#
#   FAKE_CMDLOG      file to append a record of each call to
#   FAKE_HR_LIST     file holding the HelmRelease list JSON the fleet scan returns
#   FAKE_LIST_FAIL   non-empty => the fleet scan fails
#   FAKE_PATCH_FAIL  non-empty => every patch fails
#
# Any other call fails loudly, so drift between the script and this fake does
# not pass unnoticed.
set -u

log() { printf '%s\n' "$*" >> "$FAKE_CMDLOG"; }

arg_after() { k="$1"; shift; p=""; for a in "$@"; do [ "$p" = "$k" ] && { printf '%s' "$a"; return; }; p="$a"; done; }

args="$*"

case "$args" in
  "get helmreleases.helm.toolkit.fluxcd.io --all-namespaces --output json")
    if [ -n "${FAKE_LIST_FAIL:-}" ]; then
      echo 'error: the server was unable to return a response in the time allotted' >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    cat "$FAKE_HR_LIST"
    exit 0
    ;;
  "patch helmreleases.helm.toolkit.fluxcd.io "*)
    if [ -n "${FAKE_PATCH_FAIL:-}" ]; then
      echo 'The request is invalid: the server rejected our request due to an error in our request' >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    ns=$(arg_after --namespace "$@")
    log "PATCH $ns $(arg_after "$ns" "$@") $(arg_after --type "$@") $(arg_after --patch "$@")"
    exit 0
    ;;
  "annotate configmap "*)
    log "ANNOTATE $*"
    exit 0
    ;;
  "apply --filename -")
    v=$(sed -n 's/^  version: "\{0,1\}\([0-9]\{1,\}\)"\{0,1\}$/\1/p' | head -1)
    log "STAMP ${v:-unknown}"
    exit 0
    ;;
esac

log "UNHANDLED $args"
echo "fake kubectl: unmodelled call: $args" >&2
exit 1
